		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=1175#p1175"><![CDATA[
I tried this out a few days ago and its tons of fun.  The physics and the interface are both great. Any ideas on what kind of physics engine Armadillo Run is using?  <br><br>It doesn't seem like they're using any licensed or open source library, I wonder if it runs on a full rigid body dynamics engine with constraint solvers\stacking, etc. or if its something more simple, like a Jakobsen style verlet engine.  I know Chronic Logic used a similar system for their games, so I'm assuming its the latter.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=81">Impossible</a> — Fri Jun 16, 2006 4:26 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
